--- The termination measure over an effect-bearing rule cycle, per DR-0081 §2
--- and spec/static-analysis.md. Companion to crates/whipplescript-parser/src/measure.rs.
---
--- A ranking function proves that the ring cannot turn forever: some int field
--- moves one way on every round trip toward a bound it cannot pass. That is
--- WELL-FOUNDEDNESS, and it is a different property from a bound on how many
--- turns the ring takes -- the step-bounded question, which this model does not
--- speak about because it is a question about seeds and literals rather than
--- about the ring.
---
--- The ring is abstracted to what the analysis reads:
---   hop(R, N)     rule R moves the field by N on its hop. N = 0 is a hop that
---                 carries the field through unchanged, which is legal: what has
---                 to advance is the round trip, not every step of it.
---   bounds(R)     R's guard bounds the field from the direction of travel. One
---                 anywhere on the ring is enough -- that rule stops firing once
---                 the field passes the bound, and a simple ring cannot turn
---                 without every rule on it.
---   preserves(R)  R does not consume its trigger, so the ring carries a growing
---                 population of facts rather than one token, and no single
---                 value carries a measure.
---
--- Folding consumes each token, so a state where the whole ring has been read is
--- one with no tokens left. The searches below ask for exactly the token
--- admitted as the FINAL state (=>!), which is why a premature admission cannot
--- satisfy them: it would leave unfolded hops beside it.
---
--- The model checks that:
---   * a ring that advances, is bounded, and consumes is admitted;
---   * a one-rule ring is admitted on the same terms;
---   * an unbounded ring is NEVER admitted;
---   * a ring that preserves its trigger is NEVER admitted;
---   * a ring of carry-through hops alone is NEVER admitted;
---   * a ring whose hops disagree in direction is NEVER admitted.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-TERMINATION-MEASURE is
  protecting INT .
  protecting BOOL .

  sorts Rule Cfg .

  ops ra rb : -> Rule [ctor] .

  op none : -> Cfg [ctor] .
  op __ : Cfg Cfg -> Cfg [ctor assoc comm id: none] .

  op hop : Rule Int -> Cfg [ctor] .
  op bounds : Rule -> Cfg [ctor] .
  op preserves : Rule -> Cfg [ctor] .

  --- Accumulated rise, accumulated fall, bound seen, token consumed.
  op analysis : Int Int Bool Bool -> Cfg [ctor] .
  op admitted : -> Cfg [ctor] .

  var R : Rule .
  vars N U D : Int .
  vars B C : Bool .

  crl [fold-rise] : hop(R, N) analysis(U, D, B, C) => analysis(U + N, D, B, C)
      if N > 0 .
  crl [fold-fall] : hop(R, N) analysis(U, D, B, C) => analysis(U, D + N, B, C)
      if N < 0 .
  crl [fold-carry] : hop(R, N) analysis(U, D, B, C) => analysis(U, D, B, C)
      if N == 0 .
  rl [fold-bound] : bounds(R) analysis(U, D, B, C) => analysis(U, D, true, C) .
  rl [fold-preserve] : preserves(R) analysis(U, D, B, C) => analysis(U, D, B, false) .

  --- The round trip advances in ONE direction, something bounds it, and the
  --- token is consumed. Mixed directions are not a measure: the field can move
  --- back as easily as forward and nothing descends.
  crl [admit] : analysis(U, D, B, C) => admitted
      if ((U > 0 and D == 0) or (U == 0 and D < 0)) /\ B = true /\ C = true .
endm
